  "conclusions": [
    "The auth-form password callback receives JSON from POST /api/v2/users/signin and passes it unchanged as response; its completion reads response.id and response.authToken. No nested user wrapper is introduced.",
    "The desktop UserModel for /api/v2/user defines id as an integer (Number.isInteger), and authToken, username and title as strings. Its signIn method resolves the bare object. This corroborates numeric id and string profile fields, not legacy signin or string-id response support.",
    "Momoka continues its existing JSON request-body path. The official auth-form here uses jQuery form data; no account endpoint request was sent to prove that Momoka application/json request bodies are accepted."
